s written, He gave them bread from heaven to eat.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙšThen Jesus said unto them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Moses gave you not that bread from heaven; but my Father giveth you the true bread from heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYFor the bread of God is he which cometh down from heaven, and giveth life unto the world.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ;Then said they unto him, Lord, evermore give us this bread.¦layout ªlast_verse"…¤book*§chapter«first_verse#ªlast_verse(¦verses–„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠAnd Jesus said unto them, I am the bread of life: he that cometh to me shall never hunger; and he that believeth on me shall never thirst.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ@But I said unto you, That ye also have seen me, and believe not.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeAll that the Father giveth me shall come to me; and him that cometh to me I will in no wise cast out.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWFor I came down from heaven, not to do mine own will, but the will of him that sent me.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™And this is the Father's will which hath sent me, that of all which he hath given me I should lose nothing, but should raise it up again at the last day.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§And this is the will of him that sent me, that every one which seeth the Son, and believeth on him, may have everlasting life: and I will raise him up at the last day.¦layout ªlast_verse(…¤book*§chapter«first_verse)ªlast_verse3¦verses›„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ[The Jews then murmured at him, because he said, I am the bread which came down from heaven.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒAnd they said, Is not this Jesus, the son of Joseph, whose father and mother we know? how is it then that he saith, I came down from heaven?¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙIJesus therefore answered and said unto them, Murmur not among yourselves.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnNo man can come to me, except the Father which hath sent me draw him: and I will raise him up at the last day.¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜It is written in the prophets, And they shall be all taught of God. Every man therefore that hath heard, and hath learned of the Father, cometh unto me.¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXNot that any man hath seen the Father, save he which is of God, he hath seen the Father.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNVerily, verily, I say unto you, He that believeth on me hath everlasting life.¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤text¸I am that bread of life.¦layout ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ;Your fathers did eat manna in the wilderness, and are dead.¦layout ªlast_verse1„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYThis is the bread which cometh down from heaven, that a man may eat thereof, and not die.¦layout ªlast_verse2„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÁI am the living bread which came down from heaven: if any man eat of this bread, he shall live for ever: and the bread that I will give is my flesh, which I will give for the life of the world.¦layout ªlast_verse3…¤book*§chapter«first_verse4ªlast_verse;¦verses˜„¥verse4¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^The Jews therefore strove among themselves, saying, How can this man give us his flesh to eat?¦layout ªlast_verse4„¥verse5¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’Then Jesus said unto them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Except ye eat the flesh of the Son of man, and drink his blood, ye have no life in you.¦layout ªlast_verse5„¥verse6¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiWhoso eateth my flesh, and drinketh my blood, hath eternal life; and I will 